   },
   "dice": [
    [
     {
      "t": "To recap."
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "t": "A bundle is a point in the goods space."
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "t": "The budget set is the region you can afford, and the line is its boundary."
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "t": "The intercepts come from spending your entire income on a single good."
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "t": "And the slope is the relative price, which tells you how much of one good you give up for one unit of the other."
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "t": "Change income and the line shifts; change a price and it pivots around the intercept of the good whose price did not change."
     }
    ]
   ],
